Step 3: Check if Polygon is Convex
Next, we need to check if the polygon is convex or not. A polygon is convex if it has no "dents" or "holes" within it, meaning all the interior angles are less than or equal to 180 degrees. We can check this by iterating over the edges and checking the signs of these edges.

```java
public boolean isConvex(List<Point> points) {
    int n = points.size();
    int right = 0;

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        int left = (i == 0) ? points.get(0).x : Math.min(points.get(i-1).x, points.get(i).x);
        int right = (i == n - 1) ? points.get(0).x : Math.max(points.get(n - 1).x, points.get(i+1).x);
